      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALPHA CHARLOTTE (2) is a lightly-raced but progressive mare who did well in a resuming second at Shepparton last start. That was her first outing since a debut win back in April and she'll be better for it. Should enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Big chance. ELLENS DELIGHT (1) made a strong return when she led from wider and fought on to be beaten 1.5 metres at this circuit and distance. Fitter for that and has the speed to take advantage of the inside draw. HAYCHARLI (3) overcame an early break to score by 6 metres at Goulburn last week. Draws well and could be ready to go through her grades. IM BUTTER BLUE (5) has won second-up before so can progress off the resuming fourth at Shepparton.",
